# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
# Every unit link that the package scripts of the desktop's packages make in /etc/systemd, and what
# the image does with it (image/units.sh; docs/IMAGE.md, "Services"). The image configures nothing in
# /etc, which is the user's and kept across updates:
#   usr  the same link in /usr/lib/systemd, so the unit is on with an empty /etc too
#   off  removed; our preset (80-nyra-desktop.preset) disables the unit, so the first boot does not
#        enable it again
# The build fails on a link that is not listed here, and on a listed one that no package made.
system/display-manager.service                                    usr  SDDM is the display manager: the login screen, at boot
system/graphical.target.wants/accounts-daemon.service             off  D-Bus starts it when a program asks (SDDM's user list)
system/systemd-coredump@.service.wants/drkonqi-coredump-processor@.service  off  DrKonqi's crash reports need systemd-coredump, which the base does not have
user/plasma-core.target.wants/plasma-ksmserver.service            usr  the Plasma session's session manager
user/plasma-core.target.wants/plasma-plasmashell.service          usr  the Plasma session's shell: desktop and panel
user/plasma-workspace.service                                     usr  the name the Plasma session starts its kcminit unit by
user/default.target.wants/drkonqi-coredump-cleanup.service        off  DrKonqi's crash reports (above)
user/default.target.wants/drkonqi-sentry-postman.path             off  DrKonqi sends crash reports to KDE: not without a decision
user/plasma-core.target.wants/drkonqi-coredump-pickup.service     off  DrKonqi's crash reports (above)
user/plasma-core.target.wants/drkonqi-sentry-postman.path         off  DrKonqi sends crash reports to KDE (above)
user/plasma-core.target.wants/drkonqi-sentry-postman.timer        off  DrKonqi sends crash reports to KDE (above)
user/sockets.target.upholds/drkonqi-coredump-launcher.socket      off  DrKonqi's crash reports (above)
user/sockets.target.wants/drkonqi-coredump-launcher.socket        off  DrKonqi's crash reports (above)
user/timers.target.wants/drkonqi-coredump-cleanup.timer           off  DrKonqi's crash reports (above)
user/timers.target.wants/drkonqi-sentry-postman.timer             off  DrKonqi sends crash reports to KDE (above)
system/sockets.target.wants/cups.socket                           usr  cups starts when a program or lp talks to its socket
system/multi-user.target.wants/cups.path                          usr  cups.path only watches for jobs in the spool and starts cups for them
system/multi-user.target.wants/cups.service                       off  started by its socket or path, not at boot
system/printer.target.wants/cups.service                          off  the same, for the printer target
user/default.target.wants/pipewire.service                        usr  the sound server runs in every login session
user/sockets.target.wants/pipewire.socket                         usr  PipeWire's socket, so a program that wants sound finds it
user/pipewire.service.wants/wireplumber.service                   usr  the session manager that makes devices of the sound cards, with PipeWire
user/pipewire-session-manager.service                             usr  the name PipeWire starts its session manager by (an alias of wireplumber)
user/default.target.wants/pipewire-pulse.service                  usr  the PulseAudio socket of PipeWire, which Plasma's volume control uses
user/sockets.target.wants/pipewire-pulse.socket                   usr  the same, started on first use
user/default.target.wants/filter-chain.service                    off  needs a configuration of audio filters, which nothing provides
